       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg, and I can't enter a dose above that limit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter the standard maximum of 10 mg once daily.** Usual adult dosing starts at 5 mg daily and goes up to 10 mg daily.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose.** 5 mg once daily is typical, and 2.5 mg is sometimes used for frail patients or patients with hepatic impairment.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 5 mg, I can enter that now.\n\nIf you want more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is the usual next step.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
